{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cffd6bsawh3HecPjrN9Hp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the candidate `max_copyable_motif_stretch`, and it passes the admission self-check (`OK`). Its smoke-fit ELPD-LOO was −2993.3, about 750 nats behind the best model's −2242.7. So it is a breadth probe, not a likely challenger. The comparison is rough: the smoke fit was 100 draws on one chain, and its PSIS-LOO was flagged unreliable, with 3.8% of trials above the Pareto-k tolerance.\n\n**Hypothesis:** people judge a sequence by its single most striking copyable stretch. They look for the longest run of flips that keeps repeating one short unit of 1–4 flips: a streak (HHHH), strict alternation (HTHTHT), or a repeating motif (HHTHHT, HTTTHTTT). That one stretch decides how patterned the sequence looks, and the rest of the sequence doesn't count. They pick the sequence whose most copyable stretch is shorter.\n\n**Why it fits this slot:** the brief asked for one local feature taken as a maximum over sub-sequences. The motif part targets the critique's FDR-surviving finding that people reject period-3 and period-4 repeating motifs more than the current best model predicts.\n\n**How it differs from earlier models:** the pruned `most_salient_regular_stretch` only looked at streaks and strict alternation (units of 1 and 2 flips). This model takes the maximum over units of 1–4 flips with no separate weight per kind of pattern.\n\n**Model:** the feature is, for each sequence, the number of flips in its longest repeating stretch that copying the unit would predict, divided by the sequence's length. Each person gets their own sensitivity to that feature and their own left/right lean, both drawn from population distributions with spare slots for new participants.\n\n**Not yet checked:** the self-check doesn't test novelty against the existing models, or convergence and speed under the full admission fit.\n\nAll three files are in `experiment2/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_2/`:\n- hypothesis.md\n- model_name.txt\n- candidate.py"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2460,"cache_read_input_tokens":69081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2460,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"82272f30-96a8-4456-a8d5-8a67242ea136","uuid":"be3eb909-a2ce-4573-b6fb-9290f222700d","timestamp":"2026-10-03T16:31:29.875Z","request_id":"req_011Cffd6bTXT6Am9vqMREdN4"}
